Z||000000||falconhulk||08-29-2001||07:46 AM||||Anyone know approx how many amps the fiero draws with the headlights, turn signals, radio, windows?  I want to put foglights on my car but do not want to overload the alternator!  BTW is there a good tie in point for power in the front of the car?  Do I have to run a hot wire all the way from the engine compartment?  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/i-4_b_l.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||08-29-2001||12:38 PM||||What kind of foglights are you adding?  Most will only draw about 10A max.  I have a whole crap load of electronics that are hot at all times or ignition controlled, and I have not had any battery/alternator troubles.  I do have a newer battery, but for what I know the alternator is original (223,000+ miles).<P>I would run a separate wire myself, but the fan relay will have 1 hot at all times wire.  I am not sure if there are any ignition controlled +12v wires up there, which is what I recommend hooking your lights up to so you wont accidentally leave them on.<P>Good Luck||||reg||1
Z||000002||falconhulk||08-29-2001||12:55 PM||||55 watt neon blue lights.  It will draw almost 10 amps.  Just wanted to make sure I had the clearance to do it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||08-29-2001||02:10 PM||||Actually, if you're just running one 55W neon, the current will be 4.58A, but two will run you close to 10.  You should be just fine.||||reg||1
Z||000004||falconhulk||08-29-2001||02:54 PM||||Yeah its 2 - 1 foglight would look kind of silly!  lol.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/i-4_b_l.jpg"> ||||reg||1
